Q1) A Differentiate between virus, worm, and Trojan horse. 

1.Virus.          
• Malware that attaches
to a file or program.

•Requires a host file or
program.

•Replicates by infecting
other files.

•Through infected files,
USB drives, or
downloads.

•Often requires
execution of an
infected file.

•Infect files and
potentially damage
data.

example
File-infecting virus


2.Worm

•Malware that replicates
and spreads
independently.

•Does not require a host
file.

•Replicates
automatically.

•Through networks and
vulnerable systems.

•Can spread without
direct user action.

•Spread rapidly and
disrupt systems or
networks.

Example 
Conficker worm


3.Trojan Horse

•Malware disguised as
legitimate software.

• Usually exists as a
standalone program.

• Does not usually
self-replicate.

• Through deceptive
downloads, attachments,
or applications.

• Usually requires the user
to install or run it.

• Trick users and perform
malicious activities.

•Example
Fake antivirus containing
malware

6. Prevention Methods

1. Install and regularly update antivirus software.
2. Keep the operating system and applications updated.
3. Avoid opening suspicious email attachments or links.
4. Download software only from trusted sources.
5. Use a firewall and perform regular data backups.



Q. 2 B Write a Python program to detect spam emails using predefined keywords.

spam_keywords = [
"win",
"winner",
"free",
"prize",
"lottery",
"urgent",
"offer",
"click here",
"claim",
"money",
"congratulations"
]
email = input("Enter the email message: ")
email_lower = email.lower()
spam_words_found = []
for keyword in spam_keywords:
if keyword in email_lower:
spam_words_found.append(keyword)
print("\n---------- Result ----------")
if len(spam_words_found) >= 2:
print("Email Status: SPAM")
print("Spam keywords found:", spam_words_found)
else:
print("Email Status: NOT SPAM")
print("Spam keywords found:", spam_words_found)
print("----------------------------")




